Description: Backport the speech-to-text manager of ktextaddons 2.3.0
 The 2.1.2 library loads no engine (nothing calls SpeechToTextManager::switchEngine),
 never opens the microphone (initializeInput has no caller), and its action calls into
 an engine that was never created. Laurent Montel finished the manager upstream in
 September 2026: the engine stored in the program's settings is loaded at the first
 dictation, the action starts and stops the microphone, the engine gives its result
 when the capture stops, and the action hands the text to the program (textAvailable).
 .
 These files are taken at the v2.3.0 tag and adapted to 2.1.2: the 2.1.2 entry point
 SpeechToTextManager::speechToText() stays beside speechToText(QObject *), so no symbol
 of the library goes away; the Whisper Python installer of later versions is not taken;
 the configure widget keeps its 2.1.2 form, saves through the backported helpers and
 reloads the engine; the test program is upstream's speechtotextgui.
Origin: backport, https://invent.kde.org/libraries/ktextaddons/-/tree/v2.3.0/textspeechtotext
Author: Laurent Montel
Applied-Upstream: v2.3.0; its commits 9b64b524 (implement manager), e954a928 (Allow to start/stop plugin), 69231039 (Now we can use plugins), 8752575f (Load/save engine support), 8abdd351 (Reload engine when we save settings), e47c7e2d (Update speechtotextaction as toolbutton), 725d5b80 (Add icon + update icon when we record it), all of 2026-09-15
Last-Update: 2026-11-22
